# Independent Plan toolbar press states

Eliminate the remaining shared enlargement/highlight animation between Graph and Help.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Pressing Graph enlarges or highlights only Graph, never Help.
- [ ] Pressing Help enlarges or highlights only Help, never Graph.
- [ ] Releasing either control invokes only its own action.
- [ ] Controls have separate visual/button identities outside any navigation container that couples their pressed animation.
- [ ] Graph retains its current SCR-003 navigation availability and Help retains its contextual alert.
- [ ] Both controls retain accessible labels and adequate independent hit regions.
- [ ] Interaction regression coverage compiles for taps in both directions.
- [ ] Focused pressed-state checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This supersedes TASK-018, whose separate `ToolbarItem` declarations did not fully isolate UIKit/SwiftUI enlargement feedback.
